/E (3.4 Challenges in Behavioral Interpretation)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 288 0 R
/E (One of the main challenges in autism-related behavior analysis is that similar movements may also appear in typically developing children. Context, frequency, and consistency play a significant role in distinguishing autism-related behaviors from normal activities.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 288 0 R
/E (As a result, automated systems must be designed with caution and should be considered supportive rather than diagnostic tools.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
