/E (Due to the limited size of the available dataset, data augmentation techniques were applied to improve model generalization and reduce overfitting. Several augmentation methods were used to increase data diversity while preserving the semantic meaning of autism-related behaviors. These techniques included horizontal flipping to account for directional movement variations, saturation and brightness adjustments to handle lighting differences, and slight blur to simulate motion and camera noise. The applied augmentations helped enhance the robustness of the model when dealing with real-world video data.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
